# External link icons

Sitewide, external links get a ↗ icon via `initExternalLinkIcons()` in `assets/js/scripts-*.js` (runs on load and after dynamic content).

## Do not add icons to

- **Notice board links** — `#noticeContainer`, `#masjid-notice-spotlight`, `#notice-board`
- Links with `data-skip-external-icon="true"` (set in JS as `dataset.skipExternalIcon = "true"`)

Notices open poster images in the BaguetteBox lightbox. They are not “leave the site” navigation, so a ↗ icon is misleading.

## When adding new exceptions

1. Set `data-skip-external-icon="true"` on the link in HTML or when creating it in JS, **or**
2. Extend `shouldSkipExternalLinkIcon()` with a stable container selector.

Do not disable `initExternalLinkIcons()` globally for a single section.

## Still show icons on

Footer links, Mixlr, GoFundMe, maps, register forms, programme listen links, PDF timetable, and other genuine off-site navigation.
